WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.2 · Financial Management
The organisational budget

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Budget your whole first year from real prices, and plan what you will cut if income falls short.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
An organisational budget estimates all your income and spending for the year ahead. It is a plan for the whole initiative, not just the part a funder or first customer will pay for.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Three parts of the budget

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:39.722
Expenditure: Every cost: services, people, premises, equipment, insurance, fees and a contribution to reserves. For example: Our bakery lists kitchen rent, ingredients, trainee pay, the stall and equipment: about US$48,000.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:52.533
Income, by certainty: Each source marked confirmed, likely or possible, so you see how solid your plan is. For example: Own savings of US$4,000 confirmed, about US$38,000 of sales likely, the US$6,000 youth fund pending.

7
00:00:52.533 --> 00:01:08.026
Contingency and cuts: A buffer for higher costs, and a plan for what you cut if income does not arrive. For example: If the youth fund says no, the bakery takes two trainees, not four, and keeps the stall.

8
00:01:08.426 --> 00:01:09.026
Why it matters now

9
00:01:09.026 --> 00:01:15.070
1. You have no past spending, so written assumptions are your only guide.

10
00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:21.485
2. It shows the full cost of your plan, not just one funded part.

11
00:01:21.485 --> 00:01:27.789
3. It lets you compare your plan with reality every month.

12
00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:28.789
What it guides

13
00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:34.093
1. Your project budgets, which must add up to this one.

14
00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:39.396
2. Your cash flow forecast and your monthly budget versus actual.

15
00:01:39.396 --> 00:01:45.330
3. Your prices and funding asks, based on real costs.

16
00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.330
What to avoid

17
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:51.263
Guessing costs instead of getting quotes and real prices.

18
00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:56.567
Planning spending against possible income with no plan to cut.

19
00:01:56.567 --> 00:02:02.870
Leaving out founder pay, insurance, fees or a contingency line.

20
00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.270
You write your first-year budget headings and assumptions.

21
00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:09.270
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.870
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
